## 6. Troubleshooting Quick‑Reference

| Symptom | Possible Cause | Check / Fix |
|---------|----------------|-------------|
| Motors stay silent | No voltage on EN pins | Verify `analogWrite` is called; measure EN pins with a multimeter. |
| Motor draws too much current, Arduino resets | Power supply insufficient | Use a larger battery or separate regulator; add decoupling capacitor (100 µF) across motor supply. |
| Servo jittery or stalls | Insufficient 5 V current | Power servo from an external 5 V supply, not the Arduino’s regulator. |
| Motor direction opposite of expectation | Wiring of IN pins swapped | Swap the two direction pins for the affected motor. |
| Speed knob has no effect | Potentiometer not connected to correct analog pin | Verify wiring and that `analogRead` uses the right pin number. |
| Motor makes a loud click when stopping | Flyback diode missing or reversed | Add diode across motor terminals, stripe side to positive. |

